From 7e449f6c3498cbe53cfcd683f51dc9bae34f2aa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:53:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve crate-qualified type paths in workspaces

Types were only registered as `crate::<mods>::Type`, so RON files that live
outside a crate (e.g. `assets/` at the root of a Cargo workspace) could not
name them by their real path such as `proj_core::user::User`.

While scanning, find each source file's crate (the nearest Cargo.toml with a
`[package] name`, `-` replaced by `_`) and also register its types and type
aliases under `<crate_name>::<mods>::Type`. These live in separate maps, so
same-named modules in different workspace members no longer shadow each other
for crate-qualified lookups, and `get_all_types` does not return duplicates.
Existing `crate::` and bare-name annotations behave as before.

Fixes #15
